# No Defaults

Be explicit. Do not pick a value for the caller.

- If a value changes behavior, it is required and has no default.
- A missing value raises. It does not fall back to a common or previous choice.
- Do not add a default because one value is usual in examples or docs.
- Call sites, examples, and docs pass every value they rely on.
